economia-trader has no third-party runtime dependencies (Python standard library only:
urllib, hmac, hashlib, json, decimal). The optional `hitl` extra installs hitlwright
(MIT, same author) for per-order human approval of live orders.

The core has no third-party runtime dependencies. Exchange access comes from optional extras,
installed separately and not redistributed: ccxt (MIT, crypto) and alpaca-py (Apache-2.0,
stocks). Not financial advice; trading can lose all invested capital.
